course: dictionary
lesson: 15378
title: Spayed: a word about pets
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are about everyday life, and pet care uses words you may hear at the vet or at an animal shelter. Spayed is one of them. When you meet a new word, look at the words around it for clues. «Our cat was spayed at the vet's last week.» The sentence tells you the cat went to the vet, and the next part of the sentence is about kittens.
explain: Spayed is a verb, the past tense of spay. You can also use it as an adjective: «My spayed dog is calm and happy.» Spay is the everyday word for a female animal having a vet operation so she cannot have babies. Spayed means that operation has already happened.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The shelter spayed the female dogs before they went to new homes.» If you put "had an operation so they cannot have puppies" in place of spayed, the sentence still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Spay is a verb: spay, spays, spayed, spaying.
fact: «Spayed» means that a female animal had an operation by a vet to remove the parts that make babies, so she cannot have young.
fact: A male animal has a similar operation called neutering (or castrating).
fact: Animal shelters often spay pets before they go to new homes, so there are fewer unwanted kittens and puppies.
fact: You can say «spayed and vaccinated» or «get your cat spayed», as people do when they talk about looking after pets.
exercise: «Our cat was spayed at the vet's last week.» What does spayed mean here? | *A female animal had an operation so she cannot have babies | A cat was given a new name by its owner | A cat learned to do tricks | A female animal went on holiday to the seaside
exercise: What is the word for the similar operation on a male animal? | Vaccinated | Adopted | Spayed | *Neutered
exercise: «The shelter spayed the dogs before they went to new homes.» Find and copy the word that tells what the shelter did. | homes | before | shelter | *spayed
test: Why do people get female pets spayed? | *To stop unwanted kittens or puppies | To make their fur grow longer | To teach them to fetch a ball | To make them grow taller
test: Sam says spayed means the animal is sick with a cold. Is he right? | *No, it means the operation stops her having babies | Yes, it means she is lost | No, it means she has a new name | Yes, it means she has a cold
exam: Which sentence uses spayed correctly? | *The vet spayed Bella, so she will not have puppies | The spayed sun came up over the hill | Bella spayed her dinner and then went to bed | Bella was spayed in the park on her new bike
